 The Manager, Accounting & Financial Reporting will: 
 Manage and coordinate the day-to-day accounting and financial reporting activities of the assigned team, ensuring work is completed accurately and within established timelines; 
 Assign, prioritize and monitor accounting and reporting activities to ensure appropriate workload distribution and timely completion of operational requirements; 
 Review accounting records, reconciliations, journal entries and supporting documentation prepared to ensure accuracy, completeness and compliance; 
 Support the year-end financial reporting process, including the completion and review of working papers, reconciliations, schedules and supporting documentation; 
 Provide operational guidance to university departments regarding established accounting processes, documentation requirements, reporting timelines and related financial procedures; 
 Review and respond to accounting and financial reporting inquiries, determining appropriate actions or escalating complex matters; 
 Monitor accounting and reporting processes to identify operational issues, inefficiencies, control concerns and opportunities to improve service delivery; 
 Ensure established internal controls, policies, procedures and documentation requirements are consistently applied within the assigned function; 
 Coordinate and support the design, implementation and testing of financial system integrations and related integration enhancements; 
 Provide operational information and recommendations to the Director to support decisions regarding accounting, reporting, processes and resource requirements; 
 Provide comprehensive leadership by managing, coaching, and mentoring assigned staff. 
 Key Skills and Experience: 
 An undergraduate degree or the equivalent combination of education and experience; 
 Professional Accounting Designation (CPA); 
 Financial planning, reporting, and analysis experience; 
 Experience leading a team in a finance function; 
 Knowledge of generally accepted accounting principles, financial reporting, internal controls and tax compliance; 
 Ability to identify business requirements, define strategies, develop metrics, and implement practical business solutions under deadline; 
 Ability to identify areas of risk and/or opportunity and research and develop recommendations to address; 
 Demonstrated competence with details and deadlines, with the ability to manage competing priorities; 
 Knowledge of the University environment and related practices; 
 Promotes and embodies inclusivity and respect within the workplace and the broader community; 
 Effective verbal and written communication skills, with the ability to establish and maintain sound working relationships; 
 Ability to research and develop recommendations to be applied to/solutions for complex financial problems and business processes, including developing creative solutions. 
